    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183-a1">

                <pb facs="0438" n="396" xml:id="pg396"/>

                <head>Attachment</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1966-06-20T10:30:00-04:00">June 20, 1966, 10:30 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#bold">Memorandum From the Presidentʼs Special Assistant (Rostow)
                        to President Johnson</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. President:</p>
                <p>At your suggestion Jim Thomson has prepared the attached collection of
                    imaginative initiatives with respect to Cambodia.</p>
                <p>My recommendation is that you instruct me to request Secretary Rusk to examine
                    them and make his recommendations to you—understanding, however, that you wish
                    movement on this problem.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Walt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p rendition="#flush">Approved<anchor n="2" xml:id="d183-f1"/>
                    </p>
                    <p rendition="#flush">Disapproved</p>
                    <p rendition="#flush">See me</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d183-f1" n="2" xml:id="d183-f1-content">
                <p>Johnson approved and wrote the following note: “This is excellent. Iʼm
                    proud—L.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
